Basalt Deep Learning — C++20 Deep-Learning Framework
====================================================

Basalt Deep Learning is a portable C++20 deep-learning framework built on
top of the Bellows machine-learning library.  It is licensed under the GNU
General Public License version 3 or later (see `COPYING`).

Basalt Deep Learning is an independent project; it is not part of the GNU
Project, is not endorsed by or affiliated with the Free Software Foundation,
and applies the GNU Coding Standards purely as a coding style, packaging,
and documentation discipline.

Overview
--------

Basalt Deep Learning provides:

  * N-dimensional strided tensors (`basalt::Tensor`) with broadcasting,
    multiple data types (`f16`, `bf16`, `f32`, `f64`, `i32`, `i64`, `u8`,
    `bool`), and unified CPU (SIMD/BLAS) and runtime-loaded CUDA backends.
  * Reverse-mode automatic differentiation over dynamic computation graphs,
    including higher-order gradients (`create_graph`) and `no_grad` /
    `enable_grad` scopes.
  * Neural network modules (`basalt::nn`): `Linear`, `Conv1d`, `Conv2d`,
    `Conv3d`, pooling (`Max_Pool`, `Avg_Pool`, `Adaptive_Avg_Pool`),
    normalization (`Batch_Norm`, `Layer_Norm`, `Group_Norm`, `RMS_Norm`),
    activations, `Multihead_Attention`, transformer encoder/decoder blocks,
    `Embedding`, and `Dropout`.
  * Optimizers (`SGD` with momentum and Nesterov, `Adam`, `AdamW`,
    `RMSprop`, `Adagrad`, `LAMB`) and learning-rate schedulers (`Step_LR`,
    `Cosine_Annealing_LR`, `One_Cycle_LR`, `Linear_Warmup_LR`,
    `Reduce_LR_On_Plateau`).
  * Numerically stable losses and evaluation metrics integrated with Bellows.
  * Multi-threaded prefetching data pipeline (`Dataset`, `Transform`,
    `Collate`, `Data_Loader`, and memory-mapped dataset readers).
  * Mixed-precision training (`fp16`/`bf16`), gradient scaling, gradient
    accumulation, and activation checkpointing.
  * Versioned, self-describing checkpoints with backward-compatibility
    guarantees, plus import and export of Safetensors and ONNX models.
  * Lightning-style `basalt::Trainer` with callbacks, hooks, early stopping,
    checkpoint resume, pluggable loggers, reproducible seeding, and
    multi-device data-parallel training.
  * Stable C ABI (`libbasalt-c`), command-line utilities (`basalt-train`,
    `basalt-inspect`, `basalt-convert`), and optional `pybind11` Python
    bindings (`basalt-dl` distribution, imported as `import basalt`).

Building and Installing
-----------------------

Basalt Deep Learning uses GNU Autoconf, Automake, and Libtool:

    ./configure
    make
    make check
    make install

You may specify `--with-bellows=DIR` and `--with-hyper-math=DIR` if Bellows
and Hyper Math are not installed in standard system locations or sibling
directories, and `--enable-python` to build the Python bindings.  See
`INSTALL` for standard `configure` options.

Documentation and Licensing
---------------------------

The complete reference manual is located in `doc/basalt-dl.texi` ("Basalt
Deep Learning Reference Manual") and can be built in Info, HTML, PDF, or
DVI formats via `make info`, `make html`, or `make dvi`.

For copying and licensing terms, see `COPYING`.
Bug reports should be sent to <Kival@basalt-dl.org>.
